From: hectorqin <14220132+hectorqin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 03:39:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] fix(sessions): walk child trees to any depth and batch
 them per project list

Child trees stopped at 8 levels while every attached child was still
left out of its own project, so a 9th generation showed up nowhere.
Read the whole tree with one recursive CTE (UNION ends parent loops in
damaged data; each session is placed under one parent only), using the
same visibility rule as the attachment predicate, so a session is always
either under its parent or in its own project.

The project list also read child trees and attached-child counts once
per project. Read the trees for every project's page in one query and
the counts with one GROUP BY project_path, and map them back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
